# Trivy vulnerability ignore list for mnyace-api
#
# CVE-2026-47884 / CVE-2026-47890 - Spring Framework (spring-webmvc).
# Open-source fix exists only in Spring Framework 7.0.9, which requires
# Spring Boot 4.x - an architecture-level migration, not a point upgrade.
# The Spring Boot 3.5.x line took its final OSS patch on 2026-06-30; no
# free 6.2.x backport exists (6.2.20 is Enterprise Support only).
#
# Both CVEs require code paths this app doesn't have:
#   - CVE-2026-47884: needs XsltView + an unmapped "/**" catch-all view
#     resolution. This app is REST-only - @RestController everywhere,
#     no view resolvers at all.
#   - CVE-2026-47890: needs server-rendered view fragments streamed over
#     Server-Sent Events. No SSE/fragment streaming exists in this app.
#
# Risk accepted as unreachable. Tracked for the planned Spring Boot 4
# migration - re-run Trivy after that lands and delete these two lines.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-04-01
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-04-01